Z||000000||peterh||05-24-2000||03:50 PM||||I just called the Fiero store about ordering the door weatherstriping for my car and was told it has been discontinued by GM, so no longer available. Does anyone know of where I can get these, maybe in somebodys warehouse?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-25-2000||05:47 AM||||a lot of these type of parts are common to several different cars from same manufacturer. Try a company that makes restoration parts for GTO's, Camaro/Firebirds. You may find that its the same, except you may have to cut some excess off the end. Sorry I dont have any names or companies but Ive seen them advertised on tv shows like Classic Cars on TNN. THey should be able to tell you if they interchange with Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||peterh||05-25-2000||08:29 AM||||Thanks, I have seen advertisements for GM products in the car magazines, I will try them.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||lennyb4||05-25-2000||09:00 AM||||Theres a company called JCWHITNEYS who sells all styles of weatherstripping by the foot. They have the correct stuff for the doors, trunk, hood, and other seals. I have ordered this in the past and can say its factory quality material. I think the web site is <A HREF="http://www.jcwhitney.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jcwhitney.com</A> ||||reg||1
